+ * Rather than adding a pvr-specific ioctl, the BO is exported as a dma-buf and
+ * DMA_BUF_IOCTL_SYNC is used. That lands in the exporter's begin_cpu_access() /
+ * end_cpu_access(), and the kernel's drm_gem_shmem helpers implement those with
+ * dma_sync_sgtable_for_cpu()/for_device() - exactly the maintenance needed, over
+ * the whole object. No kernel change, and it is the same path any other dma-buf
+ * consumer uses.
